  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "Strategy achieved positive gross P&L (+\u20b97.09) but suffered a net loss (\u20b9-42.27) entirely due to transaction fee drag (\u20b949.36) and correlated long-side stop-outs on 2026-10-22. Five losses hit the exact 0.68% hard stop within 5 to 75 minutes, while afternoon entries (13:45\u201314:10) lacked sufficient runway before the 15:15 EOD square-off to overcome the ~0.15% round-trip statutory fee hurdle. Additionally, Trade #4 triggered a breakeven stop that locked in a tiny gross gain (+\u20b93.32) which turned into a net loss after brokerage and STT.",
    "learning": "In small-capital NSE cash equity trading, a 0.95% target paired with a 0.68% stop yields an unfavorable net reward-to-risk ratio after ~0.15% round-trip friction; expanding targets to capture larger institutional impulse waves while tightening initial stops and requiring higher volume conviction (2.75x) filters out low-momentum midday drift and fee-bleed trades.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.35,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.75,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.15,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #25 Forensics & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing in Cycle #25 demonstrated positive gross expectancy (+\u20b97.09 gross P&L across 14 trades) that was negated by \u20b949.36 in NSE transaction costs and late-session decay. Forensics revealed cluster risk on broad trend-down days (four long losses on Oct 22) and fee-induced losses on breakeven stops and post-13:45 entries. To elevate net Profit Factor above 1.20, we are raising `min_target_pct` from 0.95% to 1.35% to amortize fixed statutory fees, tightening `min_sl_pct` from 0.68% to 0.55% to cut false-breakout losses faster, increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to 2.75x to demand genuine institutional absorption, and pushing `breakeven_trigger_r` to 1.15R to prevent premature scratches before trend expansion."
